# Adagia, Windswept Bastion's 12+ ability (CR 721.2a): "Create a token that's a copy of target artifact or enchantment you
# control, except it's legendary" (CR 707.2, 707.9b). Six counters from Lake-town Mariners on turn 1 are not enough: on turn 3
# the ability is refused with Adagia untapped and four Moxes to pay {3}{W}; a second station makes twelve and it is there.
# The token copies Mox Jet's printed values, not its tapped status (the Mox paid for the ability), and is legendary while
# the Mox it copies is not (ruling: two permanents of the same name, only the token legendary, neither put into a graveyard).
# In Bot1's upkeep on turn 5 the ability is refused - "activate only as a sorcery" - and in the main phase it copies Mox Jet
# again: two legendary Mox Jet tokens, so the legend rule (CR 704.5j) puts one into the graveyard, where a token ceases to
# exist (CR 704.5d), and the original Mox Jet stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
